---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site.ts';
---

<Layout
  title="ProtocolX Verify"
  path="/verify"
  description="Five automated CI security gates on every pull request for Sui Move packages. Generates a cryptographic SHA-256 evidence bundle anyone can re-derive."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script is:inline src="/js/canon.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="/js/dev.js" defer></script>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow-pill"><i></i>Contract Security CI &middot; Live</span>
        <h1>ProtocolX Verify</h1>
        <p class="for">Continuous assurance for engineering leads shipping Sui Move</p>
        <p class="lede">
          Audit-grade automated verification on every pull request at a fraction of manual audit cost. Five CI gates run on every commit and output a portable SHA-256 evidence bundle any customer, auditor, or exchange can verify.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#try-verifier">
            <span>Try Browser Verifier</span>
            <svg><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg>
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/contact#topic-verify">Order $1,000 First Report</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="markfig">
        <div class="markfield" data-mark="hero" data-mark-seq="mark,verify" role="img" aria-label="Animated geometric blocks forming the ProtocolX Verify mark."></div>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap" style="margin-top:clamp(36px,5vw,56px)">
      <div class="run" data-reveal>
        <div class="winbar">
          <span class="lights" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
          <span>Sample CI Output &middot; example/pkg PR #482 (illustrative)</span>
          <span class="right">bundle &middot; sha256</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rows">
          <div class="row"><span class="k">gate.01</span><span class="d"><b style="color:var(--text);font-weight:600">build</b> &mdash; Package compiles cleanly on an isolated runner with a pinned Sui CLI</span><span class="pass">[ PASS ]</span></div>
          <div class="row"><span class="k">gate.02</span><span class="d"><b style="color:var(--text);font-weight:600">digest</b> &mdash; Source reproduces the exact bytecode digest deployed on-chain</span><span class="pass">[ PASS ]</span></div>
          <div class="row"><span class="k">gate.03</span><span class="d"><b style="color:var(--text);font-weight:600">tests</b> &mdash; Full Move test suite passes against the proposed commit</span><span class="pass">[ PASS ]</span></div>
          <div class="row"><span class="k">gate.04</span><span class="d"><b style="color:var(--text);font-weight:600">pin</b> &mdash; Framework dependencies remain locked to verified revisions</span><span class="pass">[ PASS ]</span></div>
          <div class="row"><span class="k">gate.05</span><span class="d"><b style="color:var(--text);font-weight:600">mutation-smoke</b> &mdash; Deletes assertions one by one and re-runs tests to measure real suite coverage (derived, executed, killed, survived)</span><span class="pass">[ PASS ]</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="meta">
          <div><span>status</span><span class="pass">ready to merge</span></div>
          <div><span>engine</span><span>protocolx-verify &middot; self-gates</span></div>
          <div><span>digest</span><code>sha256:8f42a9c1d0b6e73f4c2e5a90b7d1e6c3ab52f7d0e9c48d31bf6a02e5d7c9a1b8</code></div>
          <div><span>re-derive</span><code>verify reproduce &lt;digest&gt;</code></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="note-mono">Every PR produces a verifiable bundle.json artifact your team and customers can independently check.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap twocol">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="cmd">Why Teams Adopt Verify</p>
        <p class="prob">Passing unit tests can leave critical balance and permission assertions untested. Between formal audits, teams lack an objective, continuous record proving every pull request was verified.</p>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="cmd">Deliverables</p>
        <ul class="gets">
          <li>Five automated CI gates on every pull request: build, digest, tests, pin, and mutation-smoke.</li>
          <li>Cryptographic SHA-256 evidence bundle attached to every run.</li>
          <li>One-line verification command for customers, exchanges, and auditors.</li>
          <li>Optional hosted runners with artifact retention and private repo support.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head" data-reveal>
        <p class="cmd">Pipeline Architecture</p>
        <h2>Five gates, one portable proof bundle.</h2>
      </div>
      <figure class="gates-fig" data-reveal>
        <div class="gates" data-gates="31,29" role="img" aria-label="Visualization of the five verification gates and mutation smoke testing."></div>
        <ul class="gate-list" style="margin-top:24px">
          <li><span class="gn">gate.01</span><span class="pass">[ PASS ]</span><span class="gd"><b>build</b>Compiles the package from scratch on a clean runner with a pinned Sui CLI</span></li>
          <li><span class="gn">gate.02</span><span class="pass">[ PASS ]</span><span class="gd"><b>digest</b>Confirms local source matches the on-chain package bytecode digest</span></li>
          <li><span class="gn">gate.03</span><span class="pass">[ PASS ]</span><span class="gd"><b>tests</b>Executes the full Move test suite against the exact PR commit</span></li>
          <li><span class="gn">gate.04</span><span class="pass">[ PASS ]</span><span class="gd"><b>pin</b>Verifies Move framework dependencies have not drifted unexpectedly</span></li>
          <li><span class="gn">gate.05</span><span class="pass">[ PASS ]</span><span class="gd"><b>mutation-smoke</b>Deletes assertions iteratively up to a set limit and records how many mutants were derived, killed, or survived</span></li>
        </ul>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="try-verifier">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head" data-reveal>
        <p class="cmd">Interactive Product Demo</p>
        <h2>Test an evidence bundle in your browser.</h2>
        <p>Edit any character in the JSON manifest on the left or drop your own <code>bundle.json</code> file. Your browser recomputes the canonical SHA-256 digest locally with zero network calls.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vbox" data-verify>
        <div class="editor">
          <div class="winbar">
            <span class="lights" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
            <span>bundle.json</span>
            <span class="right" data-count>1142 chars</span>
          </div>
          <label class="sr" for="bundle-src">Evidence bundle JSON</label>
          <textarea is:raw id="bundle-src" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off">{
  &quot;schema&quot;: &quot;protocolx-verify/evidence-manifest&quot;,
  &quot;schemaVersion&quot;: 1,
  &quot;subject&quot;: {
    &quot;repository&quot;: &quot;Northlatch-Labs-LLC/example&quot;,
    &quot;commitSha&quot;: &quot;9c1f0a2b7d4e6f8091a2b3c4d5e6f708192a3b4c&quot;,
    &quot;packagePath&quot;: &quot;move/&quot;
  },
  &quot;toolchain&quot;: {
    &quot;sui&quot;: {
      &quot;value&quot;: &quot;sui 1.44.2&quot;,
      &quot;reason&quot;: null
    },
    &quot;python&quot;: {
      &quot;value&quot;: &quot;Python 3.14.0&quot;,
      &quot;reason&quot;: null
    }
  },
  &quot;gates&quot;: {
    &quot;build&quot;: {
      &quot;status&quot;: &quot;pass&quot;,
      &quot;reason&quot;: null
    },
    &quot;digest&quot;: {
      &quot;status&quot;: &quot;pass&quot;,
      &quot;reason&quot;: null
    },
    &quot;tests&quot;: {
      &quot;status&quot;: &quot;pass&quot;,
      &quot;reason&quot;: null
    },
    &quot;pin&quot;: {
      &quot;status&quot;: &quot;pass&quot;,
      &quot;reason&quot;: null
    },
    &quot;mutation-smoke&quot;: {
      &quot;status&quot;: &quot;pass&quot;,
      &quot;reason&quot;: null,
      &quot;derivable&quot;: 31,
      &quot;limit&quot;: 40,
      &quot;derived&quot;: 31,
      &quot;executed&quot;: 31,
      &quot;killed&quot;: 29,
      &quot;survived&quot;: 2
    }
  },
  &quot;digest&quot;: {
    &quot;algorithm&quot;: &quot;sha256&quot;,
    &quot;excludes&quot;: [
      &quot;run&quot;,
      &quot;bundleDigest&quot;
    ]
  },
  &quot;run&quot;: {
    &quot;generatedAtUtc&quot;: &quot;2026-09-16T04:00:00Z&quot;
  },
  &quot;bundleDigest&quot;: &quot;sha256:a6821ad2cdf557c60a6c800ad800683dc0fc1d101b240e6762e5be330b315d52&quot;
}</textarea>
          <div class="foot">
            <button class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" type="button" data-run>Re-derive Digest</button>
            <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" type="button" data-reset>Reset Sample</button>
            <span class="faint">Or drag &amp; drop a bundle.json file</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="vresult" aria-live="polite">
          <div class="digestgrid" data-digestgrid role="img" aria-label="Visual 256-bit SHA-256 fingerprint grid."></div>
          <p class="vstatus" data-status>waiting</p>
          <div class="vline"><span>Computed locally</span><code data-computed>&mdash;</code></div>
          <div class="vline"><span>Claimed by bundle</span><code data-claimed>&mdash;</code></div>
          <p class="small faint">Modifying even one character flips roughly half of the 256 digest bits &mdash; making tampering immediately detectable.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top:32px" data-reveal>
        <p class="cmd">Supported Environments</p>
        <div class="cats">
          <span>Move on Sui</span>
          <span>GitHub Actions</span>
          <span>GitLab CI</span>
          <span>Self-Hosted Runners</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap twocol">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="cmd">Pricing Plans</p>
        <h2>Simple, transparent tiers.</h2>
        <div class="pricing" style="margin-top:20px">
          <div><span>GitHub Action (in your own CI)</span><b>Free</b></div>
          <div><span>First Report (one-shot audit output)</span><b>$1,000</b></div>
          <div><span>Hosted App (managed runners &amp; retention)</span><b>$149 / repo / month</b></div>
        </div>
        <div class="actions" style="margin-top:24px">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact#topic-verify">Get Started with Hosted App or First Report</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="cmd">Self-Serve Installation</p>
        <h2>Add to your repository in minutes.</h2>
        <div class="startcmds" style="margin-top:20px">
          <span class="lbl">1 &middot; Add one step to GitHub Actions</span>
          <div class="cline"><span class="p">$</span><code>uses: Northlatch-Labs-LLC/protocolx-verify@v1</code><button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="uses: Northlatch-Labs-LLC/protocolx-verify@v1" aria-label="Copy workflow step"><svg><use href="#i-copy"/></svg><span data-copy-label>copy</span></button></div>

          <span class="lbl">2 &middot; Or scaffold with the verified installer</span>
          <div class="cline"><span class="p">$</span><code>curl -sSL {SITE.origin}/install.sh -o install.sh &amp;&amp; bash install.sh</code><button class="copy" type="button" data-copy={`curl -sSL ${SITE.origin}/install.sh -o install.sh && bash install.sh`} aria-label="Copy command"><svg><use href="#i-copy"/></svg><span data-copy-label>copy</span></button></div>

          <span class="lbl">3 &middot; Push a commit &amp; download bundle.json</span>
          <div class="cline"><span class="p">$</span><code>git push &amp;&amp; open the check run</code><button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="git push && open the check run" aria-label="Copy command"><svg><use href="#i-copy"/></svg><span data-copy-label>copy</span></button></div>
        </div>
        <p class="small faint" style="margin-top:14px">Downloaded, then run &mdash; never piped directly to a shell. Pass <code>--check</code> to inspect without writing files.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="others">Explore more solutions: <a href="/weir">Weir Accounts</a><a href="https://protocolx.io">ProtocolX Draws</a><a href="https://gridframes.app">GridFrames Hosting</a><a href="/more">SuiNS Names &amp; Range</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
